    Bug 1968768 - Set the right flag in SetFlagsOnDefaultMailboxes. r=mkmelin

    We were accidentally setting all the flags instead of the one flag we should have set. This only
    caused a problem for folders that had no flags, since the nsMsgDBFolder code was only expect a
    single flag and did a bitwise and check to see if it had the flag already.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D252614

diff --git a/mailnews/local/src/nsLocalMailFolder.cpp b/mailnews/local/src/nsLocalMailFolder.cpp
index b4c36c20f9a..395648224a0 100644
--- a/mailnews/local/src/nsLocalMailFolder.cpp
+++ b/mailnews/local/src/nsLocalMailFolder.cpp
@@ -3011,7 +3011,7 @@ nsMsgLocalMailFolder::SetFlagsOnDefaultMailboxes(uint32_t flags) {

       // Only set the flag if the folder exists.
       if (msgFolder) {
-        rv = msgFolder->SetFlag(flags);
+        rv = msgFolder->SetFlag(folderFlag);
         NS_ENSURE_SUCCESS(rv, rv);
       }
     }
